ey are market-activity measures, not consumption indicators."},{"question":"Caveats?","answer":"Volumes are in lakh trades and may be small numbers (e.g. 0.5 lakh) for the debt segments; check units. RBI data are provisional and are revised in later releases; the dashboard keeps the latest revision seen. Counts are transactions processed by the system, not unique users or goods purchased."}],"related":[],"layer":"added","note":"Source: RBI monthly Payment System Indicators (provisional, revised in later releases). Volume is in lakh (1 lakh = 100,000 = 0.1 million) transactions; value in Rs. crore (1 crore = 10 million). Published roughly a month after the reference month; history on the RBI site starts June 2021.","scraped_at":"2026-10-30T07:24:28+00:00"}